From: iPool bring-up <dev@ipool>
Date: Mon, 28 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: rockchip: pm_domains: don't panic on idle-ack timeout

The Rockchip 6.1 BSP tree hard-panics in rockchip_pmu_set_idle_request()
whenever a power domain fails to acknowledge an idle request:

    error:
        panic("panic_on_set_idle set ...\n");

On the iPool SZ3568, powering the NPU domain (touched during IOMMU init)
times out on idle-ack, so the board panics during early boot before ever
reaching userspace. The NPU is unused on this appliance. Upstream simply
returns the timeout error; do the same so boot continues and only the
affected device fails to probe.

Downstream (meta-ipool) fix for the RK3568 SZ3568 board.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream vendor-tree debug behaviour]
---
 drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
@@ -632,7 +632,10 @@

 	return ret;
 error:
-	panic("panic_on_set_idle set ...\n");
+	/* meta-ipool: the vendor tree hard-panics on any PD idle-ack timeout
+	 * (e.g. the unused NPU domain, which won't ack on this board). Upstream
+	 * just returns the error -- do that so boot continues; the affected
+	 * device simply fails to probe instead of killing the kernel. */
 	return ret;
 }

